---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Government Transparency | Phil Burney for Commissioner"
  description="Phil Burney's platform on open, accountable government for Rutherford County District 5."
>
  <section class="section platform-hero">
    <h1>Government Transparency</h1>
    <blockquote class="platform-quote">
      "For too long, Rutherford county government has operated in the shadows and isolated from the will of the voters.  
      This has led to an erosion of public trust and erased any goodwill that the public had for the local government.
      Promoting transparency will go a long way to mending this relationship."
    </blockquote>
    <a href="/platform" class="btn btn-outline back-link">← All Platform Issues</a>
  </section>

  <section class="section platform-stack">

    <article class="card">
      <h2>Citizen Engagement</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        The people most affected by local decisions should have a real voice in making
        them. Phil is committed to making county government approachable, responsive,
        and genuinely connected to the communities it serves.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Hold monthly town halls for Phil to hear directly from residents</li>
        <li>Expand public comment opportunities before major votes</li>
        <li>Create a clear, accessible way for constituents to track commissioner actions</li>
        <li>Make commissioner meeting minutes easily accessible on the county website within 72 hours of the 
        meeting taking place </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Budget Transparency</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Rutherford County residents have a right to see how their tax dollars are spent — but
        finding past county budgets is harder than it should be. Historical budgets are difficult
        to locate, and the documents that do exist are dense and hard for anyone who is not an
        accountant to understand. 
      <ul>
        <li>Require the county to publish at least 10 years of budget history in a single, easy-to-find location on the county website</li>
        <li>Produce an annual "plain language" budget summary that breaks down spending in terms residents can actually understand</li>
        <li>Publish a clear line-item comparison each year showing how the proposed budget differs from the prior year</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="cta-inner">
      <h2>Hold your government accountable</h2>
      <p>Phil is committed to earning and keeping your trust. Help him bring open, honest leadership to District 5.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/donations" class="btn btn-primary">Support the Campaign</a>
        <a href="/platform" class="btn btn-outline-light">View All Issues</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
